# Push updates to GitHub

After you change project code for the user, commit those changes and push them to `https://github.com/NeverSMILE0825/DexTools-Extension.git` on `main`.

- This standing request is permission to commit and push after a completed code change.
- Do not commit or push when the user only asked a question, or when there is nothing to commit.
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, tokens).
- Do not update git config, skip hooks, or force-push.
- Use the existing remote `origin`. If it is missing, add `https://github.com/NeverSMILE0825/DexTools-Extension.git`.
- Stage only the files that belong to the change, then push with `git push -u origin HEAD`.

```powershell
git add page.js content.css
git commit -m "Show the current gas price beside pooled ETH."
git push -u origin HEAD
```
